3,MYTHOLOGIES OF THE GADABA TRIBES - iplmyths.blogspot.com,https://iplmyths.blogspot.com/2025/06/mythologies-of-gadaba-tribes.html,"Jun 18, 2025 · The name Gadaba seems to have been derived from the word “Gada” which is a name of the river in the region and the final syllable “ba” means belonging to. They speak Gutab and Desia dialect of the Austro-Asiatic language family. The Gadaba extensively practice shifting cultivation and they cultivate a mix variety of millets, pulses and ...","Gadaba, Bodo",Austro-Asiatic
4,An Ethnographic Manifestation of Religious Life of Gadaba ...,https://www.igntu.ac.in/eContent/IGNTU-eContent-920325410720-MA-SociologyandSocialAnthropology-4-SoubhagyaranjanPadhi-TribalDevelopment-unit-v.pdf,"Gadaba’s religious life reflected through their rich folk traditions of songs, dance, music, rituals and festivals celebrated round the year adds colourful dimensions to their very existence.","Gadaba, Bodo",Austro-Asiatic
5,MYTHOLOGIES OF THE GADABA TRIBES – World Mythology,https://indigpeople.wordpress.com/2023/05/04/mythologies-of-the-gadaba-tribes/,"May 4, 2023 · They speak Gutab and Desia dialect of the Austro-Asiatic language family. The Gadaba extensively practice shifting cultivation and they cultivate a mix variety of millets, pulses and niger.","Gadaba, Bodo",Austro-Asiatic
6,The Incredible Cultural Heritage of Gadaba Tribe of Koraput District,https://archive.org/download/gadaba_310/venki.pdf,"He further goes on to write that the Gadabas belong to the Austro-Asiatic linguistic family (Somasunderam: 1949). Though the division of Gadaba varies from person to person, on the basis of language they can be clearly divided into two groups: the Ollar Gadaba from the first group being the Dravidian speaking people and the rest from the ...","Gadaba, Bodo",Austro-Asiatic
7,The Incredible Cultural Heritage of Gadaba Tribe of Koraput District,https://www.academia.edu/102628896/The_Incredible_Cultural_Heritage_of_Gadaba_Tribe_of_Koraput_District,"Gadaba tribe constitutes 62.74% of India's total Gadaba population, emphasizing their prominence in Orissa. Gadabas are classified into five sub-divisions, including Bodo and Sana Gadabas, based on language and culture. The Gadaba community exhibits a unique blend of traditional practices and modern influences, impacting their cultural identity.","Gadaba, Bodo",Austro-Asiatic
